  "source": "Built from tests/fixtures/ios27-motion.swift with swiftc for arm64-apple-ios27.0-simulator (Xcode 27.0, 27A266a, SDK 27.0, warnings as errors) and run on the iPhone 18 Pro simulator (ECD19CCB-2BD2-4361-804C-7496085499F9, iOS 27.0), light appearance, status bar overridden to 9:41; one launch per screen with -screen <name>, on 2026-10-15. Each screen changes on its own 1.5 s after launch inside withAnimation(.linear(duration: 4)), and changes back 7 s later. Screenshots were taken back to back with simctl io screenshot (each takes 0.4 to 2 s), and each is timed by the screen's own clock: a black bar 300 pt wide at the end of the change, grown or shrunk in the same transaction, so progress is its width over 300. Kept here is the screenshot nearest half way, for showing (in) and for hiding (out). The roll of the numeric screens is over in about half a second whatever the transaction's duration, so those frames come from simctl io recordVideo, read with AVAssetImageGenerator and timed by the same clock. The curves come from the curves screen: an Animatable modifier's body logs the value it is drawn with on each frame (about 60 a second), and withAnimation's completion logs when each animation is logically complete and when it is removed. 1206x2622 pixels / 402x874 points at 3x.",
