    "unanimated": {
      "note": "A .transition(.scale) with no animation: the box is there, whole, in the first screenshot after the change, and gone in the first after it is hidden. Nothing plays."
    },
    "valueOnlyChild": {
      "note": ".animation(.linear(duration: 4), value: shown) on a VStack holding only the if: the box fades in and out (opacity p) although nothing else is in what the modifier wraps, and the green bar, outside it, jumps at once (to 404.33, and back to 284.33, because the empty VStack keeps its slot and the spacing beside it)."
    },
    "numericText": {
      "note": ".contentTransition(.numericText()): each digit that changes rolls, in about half a second whatever the duration of the transaction (here 4 s linear): the old digit moves up about a third of the font size, blurring and fading, and the new one comes up from as far below, sharpening, with a slight overshoot; the first digit starts a frame or two before the next. Counting down from 10 to 9 rolls up too. numericText(value:) rolls up when the value grows and down when it shrinks.",
      "rollSeconds": 0.5,
      "travelOfFontSize": 0.35,
      "blurAtStart": 10
    },
    "textCrossFade": {
      "note": "Text whose string changes inside withAnimation, with .contentTransition(.opacity) or with no content transition at all: the old string fades out where it was and the new one fades in where it is, with the transaction's timing. The two look the same."
    },
